`]}),e.jsxs(a,{title:"Kernels, launches and where a custom kernel can help",children:[e.jsx(s.p,{children:"A GPU kernel is a function that runs on the GPU. The host program on the CPU launches it over a grid of threads. Every thread runs the same function and uses its own index to choose its data. One launch starts thousands of threads."}),e.jsx(s.p,{children:"An operation on CUDA tensors in PyTorch queues one or more kernel launches. An operation that only changes metadata, such as a view, launches none."}),e.jsxs(s.p,{children:["Standard calls such as ",e.jsx(s.code,{children:"torch.softmax"})," and matrix multiplication already run optimized kernels, so rewriting one of them in a lower-level language rarely helps by itself. The opportunity is usually a composition boundary: several operations launch separately, and each writes an intermediate tensor to HBM that the next reads back. The data could have stayed on the chip instead. Week 4 showed that FlashAttention wins by never writing the attention score and probability matrices to HBM ",e.jsx(t,{id:"dao2022flashattention",children:"Dao et al., 2022"}),". The row softmax is a simpler operation with the same kind of boundary."]})]})]}),e.jsxs(r,{title:"Five operations move four times the bytes of one",accent:4,number:"4",children:[e.jsx(i,{math:"\\text{traffic ratio} \\;=\\; \\frac{8 \\text{ passes (decomposed)}}{2 \\text{ passes (fused)}} \\;=\\; 4\\times",label:"(1)"}),e.jsxs(s.ul,{children:[`
