`]}),e.jsxs(a,{title:"Softmax's intensity, its roof, and when fusion does not pay",children:[e.jsx(s.p,{children:"Per element, a fused softmax, which reads once and writes once, performs about five operations: a comparison for the maximum, a subtraction, an exponential, an addition for the sum and a multiplication by the reciprocal. In bf16 it moves 4 bytes per element, 2 read and 2 written. The resulting 1.25 FLOP per byte is an estimate, because the exponential runs on the special-function unit (SFU) and FLOP conventions differ. The chart's marker uses Week 4's teaching value of 2 FLOP/byte."}),e.jsxs(s.p,{children:["The roof drawn in the chart is Week 4's, the H100 SXM's dense bf16 Tensor Core peak of 989.5 TFLOP/s. Softmax contains no matrix product, so it cannot use Tensor Cores. The roof that applies to softmax is the fp32 peak of 67 TFLOP/s ",e.jsx(t,{id:"nvidia2022h100datasheet",children:"NVIDIA, 2022"}),". That puts its ridge at 67 / 3.35 = 20 FLOP/byte."]}),e.jsx(s.p,{children:"For the tensor of slide 4, the lower bound for moving the bytes is about 16 times the lower bound for the arithmetic, by our own count. Removing full-tensor passes is the lever."}),e.jsx(o,{title:"Two lower bounds for this tensor",children:e.jsx(s.p,{children:"The arithmetic takes at least 5 × 134 × 10⁶ / (67 × 10¹²) ≈ 10 µs. Moving 268 MB in and 268 MB out at 3.35 TB/s takes at least 160 µs."})}),e.jsx(s.p,{children:"Fusion does not always pay. A small tensor can stay in the L2 cache (50 MB on the H100 SXM), so its intermediates never reach HBM. The traffic count then overstates the saving, and launch overhead dominates. A compute-bound operation, such as a large matrix multiplication, is limited by its arithmetic, so removing bytes changes little. A chain of launches in a profile is therefore only a candidate. The case for fusion is strong when the chain is memory-bound, its intermediates reach HBM, and the compiler leaves the boundary in place."})]})]}),e.jsxs(r,{title:"Library and compiler before a custom kernel",accent:6,number:"6",items:"5",children:[e.jsxs(s.ul,{children:[`
